<p dir=3D"auto">Global variables are declared outside of a function or decl=
ared with a window object for accessibility throughout the program (unless =
shadowed by locals). If you declare a variable without using var, even if i=
t's inside a function, it will still be seen as global.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">The <code>var</code> <strong>statement</strong> declares a =
function-scoped or globally-scoped variable, optionally initializing it to =
a value.</p>
