<p dir=3D"auto">The double exclamation mark (<code>!!</code>) in JavaScript=
 forces any value into its corresponding strict boolean representation (<co=
de>true</code> or <code>false</code>). The <code>!!</code> (double negation=
) operator converts any value to its boolean equivalent:</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>First <code>!</code> negates the value (converting it to a boolean)</li=
>
<li>Second <code>!</code> negates it again, giving the true boolean represe=
ntation</li>
</ul>
