<p dir=3D"auto">Variable shadowing occurs when a variable declared within a=
 certain scope (decision block, method, or inner class) has the same name a=
s a variable declared in an outer scope. This outer variable is said to be =
shadowed.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">If there is a variable in the global scope, and you'd like =
to create a variable with the same name in a function. The variable in the =
inner scope will temporarily shadow the variable in the outer scope.</p>
