</tr>
<tr>
<td>The null value is a primitive value that represents the null, empty, or=
 non-existent reference.</td>
<td>The undefined value is a primitive value used when a variable has not b=
een assigned a value.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Indicates the absence of a value for a variable</td>
<td>Indicates absence of variable itself</td>
</tr>
<tr>
