<p dir=3D"auto">The <strong>nullish coalescing operator</strong> (<code>??<=
/code>) returns the right-hand side operand when the left-hand side operand=
 is <code>null</code> or <code>undefined</code>. Otherwise, it returns the =
left-hand side operand. Unlike <code>||</code>, it does <strong>not</strong=
> treat <code>0</code>, <code>false</code>, or <code>""</code> as falsy.</p=
>
