<p dir=3D"auto">JavaScript does not have built-in associative arrays in the=
 way languages like PHP or literal dictionary structures do. Instead, JavaS=
cript uses regular Objects or Maps to handle key-value pairs (associative b=
ehavior).</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Associative arrays are basically objects in JavaScript wher=
e indexes are replaced by user-defined keys. They do not have a length prop=
erty like a normal array and cannot be traversed using a normal for loop.</=
p>
