<p dir=3D"auto">Both <code>for..of</code> and <code>for..in</code> statemen=
ts iterate over lists; the values iterated on are different though, <code>f=
or..in</code> returns a <strong>list of keys</strong> on the object being i=
terated, whereas <code>for..of</code> returns a <strong>list of values</str=
ong> of the numeric properties of the object being iterated.</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li><strong>for in</strong>: iterates over all enumerable properties of an =
object that are <strong>keyed</strong> by strings.</li>
<li><strong>for of</strong>: iterates over the <strong>values</strong> of a=
n iterable objects. including: built-in <code>String</code>, <code>Array</c=
ode>, array-like objects (e.g., <code>arguments</code> or <code>NodeList</c=
ode>), <code>TypedArray</code>, <code>Map</code>, <code>Set</code>, and <co=
de>user-defined</code> iterables.</li>
</ul>
