<p dir=3D"auto">One potential pitfall of using <code>new Array()</code> is =
that it can be ambiguous when you pass a single argument to the constructor=
. For example, <code>new Array(3)</code> creates an array with a length of =
3, but <code>new Array("3")</code> creates an array with a single element, =
the string "3". This is because the argument is treated as the value of the=
 first element when it's a non-negative integer, but as the length of the a=
rray when it's a string or a negative integer.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">In summary, <code>[]</code> is the preferred way to create =
a new array in JavaScript, while <code>new Array()</code> is an alternative=
 way that can be used when you need more control over the array's length or=
 contents.</p>
