<p dir=3D"auto">A <code>switch</code> statement compares a single expressio=
n against multiple discrete values using <strong>strict equality (<code>=3D=
=3D=3D</code>)</strong>. It is preferable over <code>if...else if</code> wh=
en:</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>You are comparing <strong>one variable</strong> against <strong>many po=
ssible literal values</strong>.</li>
<li>Readability is a priority (avoids repetitive condition checks against t=
he same variable).</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Pitfall =E2=80=94 Fall-through:</strong> Without a =
<code>break</code> statement, execution "falls through" to the next <code>c=
ase</code>, which is a common source of bugs.</p>
