<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Real-World Use Case:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">When consuming third-party REST APIs or GraphQL responses, =
deeply nested fields may be absent depending on the query. Optional chainin=
g eliminates dozens of guard clauses like <code>if (response &amp;&amp; res=
ponse.data &amp;&amp; response.data.user)</code>. Nullish coalescing is cri=
tical when a user-configurable setting has <code>0</code> or <code>""</code=
> as a valid value =E2=80=94 falling back with <code>||</code> would incorr=
ectly override those legitimate settings.</p>
