<p dir=3D"auto">JavaScript's logical operators (<code>&amp;&amp;</code>, <c=
ode>||</code>, <code>??</code>) use <strong>short-circuit evaluation</stron=
g>: the right-hand operand is only evaluated if necessary. This is not just=
 a performance optimization =E2=80=94 it is a widely used <strong>control f=
low</strong> mechanism.</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Operator</th>
<th>Short-circuits when left side is</th>
<th>Returns</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>&amp;&amp;</code> (AND)</td>
<td><strong>falsy</strong></td>
<td>Left operand (skips right)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>||</code> (OR)</td>
<td><strong>truthy</strong></td>
<td>Left operand (skips right)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>??</code> (Nullish)</td>
<td><strong>not null/undefined</strong></td>
<td>Left operand (skips right)</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
