<p dir=3D"auto">An arrow function is a shorter syntax for a function expres=
sion and does not have its own <strong>this, arguments, super, or new.targe=
t</strong>. These function are best suited for non-method functions, and th=
ey cannot be used as constructors.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Arrow functions in ES6 has two limitations:</strong=
></p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Do not work with new</li>
<li>Fixed this bound to scope at initialisation</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>When should not use Arrow Functions:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>1. Object methods:</strong></p>
