<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>JavaScript function objects</strong> are used to de=
fine a piece of JavaScript code. This code can be called within a JavaScrip=
t code as and when required.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Javascript Function Objects Property:</strong></p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Name</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>arguments</td>
<td>An array corresponding to the arguments passed to a function.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>arguments.callee</td>
<td>Refers the currently executing function.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>arguments.length</td>
<td>Refers the number of arguments defined for a function.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>constructor</td>
<td>Specifies the function that creates an object.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>length</td>
<td>The number of arguments defined by the function.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>prototype</td>
<td>Allows adding properties to a Function object.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
