<p dir=3D"auto">Currying is the process of taking a function with multiple =
arguments and turning it into a sequence of functions each with only a sing=
le argument.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">In other words, when a function, instead of taking all argu=
ments at one time, takes the first one and return a new function that takes=
 the second one and returns a new function which takes the third one, and s=
o forth, until all arguments have been fulfilled.</p>
