<p dir=3D"auto">Memoization is a programming technique which attempts to in=
crease a function's performance by <strong>caching</strong> its previously =
computed results.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Each time a memoized function is called, its parameters are=
 used to index the cache. If the data is present, then it can be returned, =
without executing the entire function. Otherwise the function is executed a=
nd then the result is added to the cache.</p>
