<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Recursion vs Iteration</strong>:</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Recursion is more readable for <strong>tree/graph traversal, nested str=
uctures, and divide-and-conquer</strong> problems</li>
<li>Iteration is more performant for <strong>simple loops</strong> =E2=80=
=94 use it when recursion depth could be large</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"auto"><em>Note: For deeply nested structures, iterative solutions=
 with an explicit stack are preferred over recursion to avoid stack-overflo=
w errors.</em></p>
