<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Real-World Use Case:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">In large React/Node.js codebases, <code>var</code> inside <=
code>for</code> loops iterating over async operations (e.g., firing multipl=
e API calls) was a notorious source of race-condition bugs because all call=
backs shared the same <code>i</code>. Migrating to <code>let</code> (or clo=
sure-capturing patterns) eliminated entire categories of production bugs. E=
SLint's <code>no-var</code> rule enforces this at scale.</p>
