<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Real-World Use Case:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">TDZ prevents a subtle bug in module initialisation cycles. =
If module A imports from module B and module B imports from module A, <code=
>const</code> exports are protected by TDZ, causing a clear <code>Reference=
Error</code> at the problematic access point rather than silently producing=
 <code>undefined</code> computations that corrupt data =E2=80=94 making cir=
cular-dependency bugs far easier to diagnose in large monorepo setups.</p>
