<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Real-World Use Case:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Before ES modules became ubiquitous, large libraries like j=
Query, Lodash, and early Angular 1.x used the Module Pattern (IIFE + closur=
e) to avoid polluting the global namespace and to encapsulate internal stat=
e. Today, ES modules provide file-level encapsulation, but the closure-base=
d pattern is still used inside modules for class-alternative encapsulation =
and for factories returned from hooks or composables.</p>
