<p dir=3D"auto">A closure memory leak occurs when a closure unintentionally=
 keeps a large object (such as a DOM node, a large dataset, or a complete H=
TTP response) in memory by holding a reference in its closed-over scope lon=
g after the object is needed. The V8 garbage collector cannot reclaim the m=
emory because the closure is still reachable.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Common patterns that cause leaks:</p>
<ol dir=3D"auto">
<li><strong>Event listeners not removed</strong> =E2=80=94 the listener clo=
ses over component state, keeping the entire component tree alive.</li>
<li><strong>Timers not cleared</strong> =E2=80=94 <code>setInterval</code> =
callbacks closing over large objects run indefinitely.</li>
<li><strong>Detached DOM nodes</strong> =E2=80=94 a closure holds a referen=
ce to a DOM node that has been removed from the document.</li>
</ol>
