<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>When to still use IIFEs over ES modules:</strong></=
p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li><strong>Browser script tags without a bundler</strong> =E2=80=94 when y=
ou cannot use <code>type=3D"module"</code> and need scope isolation.</li>
<li><strong>Polyfill / library UMD bundles</strong> =E2=80=94 output format=
 used by tools like Rollup/Webpack to expose libraries as <code>window.MyLi=
b</code> while avoiding global pollution.</li>
<li><strong>Initialisation code that must run exactly once</strong> and sho=
uld not be importable.</li>
<li><strong>Micro-optimisation in hot paths</strong> =E2=80=94 in rare engi=
ne-specific scenarios, an IIFE can help the optimiser treat a block as a se=
parate compilation unit.</li>
</ul>
