<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Real-World Use Case:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">In Node.js request handlers that process millions of reques=
ts per minute (e.g., an Express.js API gateway), middleware functions close=
 over the <code>app</code> config object. Profiling with <code>--prof</code=
> (V8 tick profiler) or Chrome DevTools' flame graph reveals when heap cont=
exts from closures apply GC pressure. The optimisation is to destructure on=
ly required config fields at the module level =E2=80=94 keeping the closure=
 context objects small and promoting faster minor GC cycles.</p>
