<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Real-World Use Case:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">React class components historically required <code>.bind(th=
is)</code> in the constructor for event handlers because a regular function=
 passed as a JSX prop loses its <code>this</code> binding. The shift to arr=
ow function class fields (<code>handleClick =3D () =3D&gt; { ... }</code>) =
and then to functional components with hooks eliminated this entire categor=
y of <code>this</code>-related bugs =E2=80=94 demonstrating that understand=
ing the scope vs. context distinction is foundational to making informed de=
cisions about component architecture.</p>
