<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Real-World Use Case:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">In large React component files, developers often define hel=
per arrow functions (<code>const formatDate =3D (d) =3D&gt; ...</code>) aft=
er the component function that uses them. Because the component is a <code>=
const</code> arrow function itself, calling <code>formatDate</code> inside =
it only works if <code>formatDate</code> is defined above =E2=80=94 otherwi=
se a <code>ReferenceError</code> occurs at module load time. Understanding =
hoisting rules guides file organisation: place utility declarations before =
their consumers, or use function declarations when ordering flexibility mat=
ters.</p>
