<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Real-World Use Case:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">When splitting large Node.js services into files with circu=
lar <code>require()</code> references, class-based modules that are accesse=
d during the <code>require()</code> cycle before the class declaration eval=
uates throw <code>ReferenceError</code>. Understanding the TDZ for classes =
helps engineers design module load order carefully =E2=80=94 or avoid circu=
lar dependencies by refactoring to dependency injection patterns (e.g., pas=
sing the class as a parameter rather than importing it at the module level)=
.</p>
