<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Real-World Use Case:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">This exact bug has appeared in production Redux reducers wh=
ere developers switched from <code>var</code> to <code>let</code> during a =
linting migration. All <code>case</code> branches in a reducer's <code>swit=
ch</code> share one block, so re-declaring <code>let draft</code> in multip=
le cases causes a <code>SyntaxError</code> caught only at parse time =E2=80=
=94 blocking the entire app from loading. The standard Redux Toolkit soluti=
on is to use Immer-based <code>createSlice</code> instead, which replaces t=
he <code>switch</code> reducer pattern entirely.</p>
