<p dir=3D"auto">Arrow functions (<code>=3D&gt;</code>) introduced in ES2015=
 are a concise syntax for writing functions, but they are <strong>not</stro=
ng> simply shorthand for <code>function</code>. They have fundamental seman=
tic differences:</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Feature</th>
<th>Regular Function</th>
<th>Arrow Function</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>this</code> binding</td>
<td>Dynamic =E2=80=94 determined by call site</td>
<td>Lexical =E2=80=94 inherits from enclosing scope</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>arguments</code> object</td>
<td>Available</td>
<td>Not available (use rest params)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>new</code> (constructor)</td>
<td>Can be used</td>
<td>Throws <code>TypeError</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>prototype</code> property</td>
<td>Has one</td>
<td><code>undefined</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>super</code> / <code>new.target</code></td>
<td>Own binding</td>
<td>Inherited from enclosing scope</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Method shorthand</td>
<td>Usable (with caution)</td>
<td>Avoid for object methods needing <code>this</code></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>When NOT to use arrow functions:</strong></p>
<ol dir=3D"auto">
<li><strong>Object methods</strong> that need dynamic <code>this</code> (<c=
ode>obj.method()</code> =E2=80=94 arrow's <code>this</code> is the enclosin=
g scope, not <code>obj</code>).</li>
<li><strong>Constructor functions</strong> =E2=80=94 arrow functions cannot=
 be called with <code>new</code>.</li>
<li><strong>Event handlers</strong> that need <code>this</code> to refer to=
 the DOM element (<code>element.addEventListener('click', () =3D&gt; {})</c=
ode> =E2=80=94 <code>this</code> is the outer context, not the element).</l=
i>
<li><strong>Generator functions</strong> =E2=80=94 arrow syntax does not su=
pport <code>function*</code>.</li>
<li><strong>Functions that need their own <code>arguments</code> object</st=
rong>.</li>
</ol>
