<p dir=3D"auto">Template literals (backtick strings) introduced in ES2015 o=
ffer four key capabilities over traditional string literals:</p>
<ol dir=3D"auto">
<li><strong>String interpolation</strong> =E2=80=94 embed any expression wi=
th <code>${expr}</code>.</li>
<li><strong>Multi-line strings</strong> =E2=80=94 newlines are literal; no =
<code>\n</code> needed.</li>
<li><strong>Expression evaluation</strong> =E2=80=94 any valid JavaScript e=
xpression inside <code>${}</code> including ternaries, function calls, and =
arithmetic.</li>
<li><strong>Tagged templates</strong> =E2=80=94 a function (tag) is called =
with the string parts and interpolated values, enabling domain-specific lan=
guages (DSLs), sanitisation, and localisation.</li>
</ol>
