<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Real-World Use Case:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">The <code>styled-components</code> and <code>emotion</code>=
 CSS-in-JS libraries are built entirely on tagged template literals. When y=
ou write <code>styled.div`color: ${props =3D&gt; props.primary ? 'blue' : '=
grey'};`</code>, the library's tag function receives the static CSS parts a=
nd the dynamic value functions, generates a unique class name, injects a <c=
ode>&lt;style&gt;</code> rule, and tracks theme changes =E2=80=94 all witho=
ut any custom parser. This demonstrates that tagged templates can implement=
 fully featured DSLs (CSS, GraphQL, SQL, i18n) natively in JavaScript with =
zero dependencies.</p>
