<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Real-World Use Case:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Redux reducers use object spread to produce new state immut=
ably without mutating the existing state object =E2=80=94 a requirement of =
Redux's change-detection mechanism: <code>return { ...state, isLoading: fal=
se, data: action.payload }</code>. This replaces <code>Object.assign({}, st=
ate, { isLoading: false })</code> with far more readable syntax. The V8 eng=
ine optimises spread-based object cloning with the same hidden-class mechan=
isms as <code>Object.assign</code>, so there is no meaningful performance d=
ifference in most application code.</p>
