<p dir=3D"auto">Express.js middleware factories and database client factory=
 functions (e.g., <code>createPool({ max =3D 10, idleTimeout =3D 30_000, ss=
l =3D false } =3D {})</code>) use default parameters combined with destruct=
uring to define safe, self-documenting APIs. When a downstream service call=
s the factory without all options, sensible defaults keep the service runni=
ng. The <code>=3D {}</code> on the destructured parameter is critical =E2=
=80=94 without it, calling <code>connect()</code> (no argument at all) thro=
ws <code>TypeError: Cannot destructure property 'host' of undefined</code>.=
</p>
