<p dir=3D"auto"><code>Symbol</code> is a primitive type introduced in ES6 t=
hat produces a <strong>guaranteed-unique</strong> value each time it is cal=
led, even with the same description string. Symbols are primarily used as:<=
/p>
<ol dir=3D"auto">
<li><strong>Unique property keys</strong> =E2=80=94 prevent accidental prop=
erty name collisions, especially in library/framework code that augments us=
er objects.</li>
<li><strong>Well-known Symbols</strong> =E2=80=94 <code>Symbol.iterator</co=
de>, <code>Symbol.toPrimitive</code>, <code>Symbol.hasInstance</code>, etc.=
 =E2=80=94 hooks into JavaScript's built-in protocols.</li>
</ol>
<p dir=3D"auto"><code>Symbol.iterator</code> is the well-known Symbol that =
makes any object <strong>iterable</strong> =E2=80=94 compatible with <code>=
for...of</code>, spread (<code>...</code>), destructuring, <code>Array.from=
()</code>, and other iteration consumers.</p>
