<p dir=3D"auto">Event bubbling is a type of event propagation where the eve=
nt first triggers on the innermost target element, and then successively tr=
iggers on the ancestors (parents) of the target element in the same nesting=
 hierarchy till it reaches the outermost DOM element.</p>
