<p dir=3D"auto"><code>requestAnimationFrame()</code> is a browser API that =
tells the browser to call a specified function before the next repaint. It =
is the recommended way to create smooth animations and visual updates becau=
se it synchronizes with the browser's refresh rate (typically 60 fps), avoi=
ds unnecessary renders when the tab is hidden, and does not block the main =
thread.</p>
