<p dir=3D"auto">There are three main types of errors that can occur while c=
ompiling a JavaScript program: <strong>syntax errors</strong>, <strong>runt=
ime errors</strong> ( also called <strong>exceptions</strong> ), and <stron=
g>logical errors</strong>. When an exception occurs, an object representing=
 the error is created and thrown. The JavaScript language defines seven typ=
es of built-in error objects.</p>
