<p dir=3D"auto">The browser fires a <strong><code>storage</code> event</str=
ong> on the <code>window</code> object of <strong>all other tabs/windows</s=
trong> at the same origin whenever <code>localStorage</code> is modified. T=
he tab that made the change does <strong>not</strong> receive the event its=
elf. This makes <code>localStorage</code> a lightweight broadcast channel f=
or cross-tab state synchronisation without a server.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">The <code>StorageEvent</code> object provides:</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
