<p dir=3D"auto"><code>localStorage</code> is <strong>synchronous</strong> =
=E2=80=94 every <code>getItem</code>, <code>setItem</code>, and <code>remov=
eItem</code> call <strong>blocks the main thread</strong>. In V8, these are=
 cross-process IPC calls to the browser's storage process, and while they a=
re typically fast (sub-millisecond for small payloads), they become a measu=
rable bottleneck when:</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Storing large JSON blobs (&gt;100 KB per entry)</li>
<li>Iterating all keys to find entries</li>
<li>Calling storage APIs inside animation loops or scroll handlers</li>
<li>Operating on low-end Android devices where I/O is slower</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Comparison of client-side storage options:</strong>=
</p>
