<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>2. Fetch():</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Fetch allows to make network requests similar to <code>XMLH=
ttpRequest</code>. Fetch makes it easier to make asynchronous requests and =
handle responses better than with the older XMLHttpRequest. It is an improv=
ement over the <code>XMLHttpRequest</code> API. The main difference between=
 <code>Fetch()</code> and <code>XMLHttpRequest()</code> is that the Fetch A=
PI uses Promises, hence avoiding <strong>callback hell</strong>.</p>
