<p dir=3D"auto">A <code>fetch()</code> function is available in the global =
window object. The fetch() function takes one mandatory argument, the path =
to the resource you want to fetch. It returns a Promise, whether it is succ=
essful or not. If request is successful <code>.then()</code> function will =
receive Response object, if request fails then <code>.catch()</code> functi=
on will receive an error object</p>
