<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Common CORS errors:</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li><code>No 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' header is present</code> =E2=80=
=94 server does not permit the request origin.</li>
<li><code>CORS policy: credential flag is 'true' but the 'Access-Control-Al=
low-Origin' is '*'</code> =E2=80=94 wildcard origin cannot be used with <co=
de>credentials: 'include'</code>.</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"auto"><em>Note: CORS is enforced by the browser. Server-to-server=
 calls (Node.js, curl) are not subject to CORS.</em></p>
