<p dir=3D"auto">JavaScript is <strong>single-threaded</strong> =E2=80=94 it=
 can execute only one task at a time. The <strong>event loop</strong> is th=
e mechanism that allows JavaScript to perform non-blocking I/O operations (=
like network requests and timers) despite this single-thread constraint.</p=
>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>How it works:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overf=
low-auto"><pre class=3D"notranslate"><code>Call Stack       Web APIs / Node=
 APIs       Callback Queue / Microtask Queue
