<ol dir=3D"auto">
<li>Synchronous code runs on the <strong>call stack</strong> first.</li>
<li>Async operations (e.g. <code>setTimeout</code>, <code>fetch</code>) are=
 handed off to Web APIs.</li>
<li>When complete, their callbacks are pushed to a <strong>queue</strong>.<=
/li>
<li>The event loop continuously checks: <em>"Is the call stack empty?"</em>=
 =E2=80=94 if yes, it dequeues the next callback and pushes it onto the sta=
ck.</li>
</ol>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Microtask queue vs. macro-task queue:</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li><strong>Microtasks</strong> (Promises <code>.then</code>/<code>.catch</=
code>, <code>queueMicrotask</code>, <code>MutationObserver</code>) are proc=
essed <strong>before</strong> the next macro-task.</li>
<li><strong>Macro-tasks</strong> (setTimeout, setInterval, I/O) are process=
ed one per event-loop tick.</li>
</ul>
