<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>2. Mark-and-Sweep algorithm (modern)</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">The modern approach used by all major engines (V8, SpiderMo=
nkey):</p>
<ol dir=3D"auto">
<li><strong>Mark phase</strong> =E2=80=94 starting from GC roots (<code>win=
dow</code>, global scope, call-stack variables), traverse all reachable obj=
ects and mark them.</li>
<li><strong>Sweep phase</strong> =E2=80=94 free all unmarked (unreachable) =
objects.</li>
</ol>
<p dir=3D"auto">Circular references are handled correctly because the cycle=
 is unreachable from the root after both <code>obj1</code> and <code>obj2</=
code> go out of scope.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Common causes of memory leaks in JavaScript:</stron=
g></p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Cause</th>
<th>Example</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Global variables</td>
<td>Accidentally using <code>x =3D 1</code> without <code>let/const/var</co=
de></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Forgotten timers</td>
<td><code>setInterval</code> never cleared</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Detached DOM nodes</td>
<td>DOM element removed but reference kept in a closure</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Closures retaining large objects</td>
<td>A closure captures a large array it no longer needs</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Unreleased event listeners</td>
<td><code>addEventListener</code> without a matching <code>removeEventListe=
ner</code></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
