<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Real-World Use Case:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Express.js does not natively catch errors thrown from <code=
>async</code> route handlers =E2=80=94 the error must be passed to <code>ne=
xt(err)</code> explicitly. A common production pattern is a wrapper utility=
 that bridges <code>async</code>/<code>await</code> errors into Express's e=
rror middleware:</p>
