<p dir=3D"auto">An <strong>async generator</strong> (<code>async function*<=
/code>) is a function that produces values asynchronously via <code>yield</=
code>. Each <code>yield</code> pauses execution until the consumer calls <c=
ode>.next()</code>, which returns <code>Promise&lt;{ value, done }&gt;</cod=
e>. <code>for await...of</code> is the idiomatic consumer =E2=80=94 it auto=
matically awaits each <code>.next()</code> call, making streaming processin=
g look synchronous.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">This pattern enables <strong>lazy, backpressure-aware</stro=
ng> pipelines: data is produced and consumed one chunk at a time rather tha=
n loading an entire dataset into memory.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Example:</strong></p>
