<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Real-World Use Case:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Node.js 18+ natively supports async iteration over <code>fe=
tch</code> response bodies: <code>for await (const chunk of response.body)<=
/code>. AWS S3 SDK v3 returns async iterables for <code>ListObjectsV2Comman=
d</code> pagination. OpenAI's streaming chat completions API returns a <cod=
e>ReadableStream</code> consumed with <code>for await...of</code> =E2=80=94=
 each chunk contains a token as it is generated, enabling real-time streami=
ng UIs (like ChatGPT's typing effect). Without async generators, this would=
 require complex recursive <code>.then()</code> chains or event emitter plu=
mbing.</p>
