<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Real-World Use Case:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Vue.js's <code>nextTick()</code> API was historically imple=
mented as a microtask (using <code>Promise.then</code> internally). This gu=
arantees that DOM mutations triggered by reactive data changes are fully fl=
ushed and the DOM updated before the <code>nextTick</code> callback fires =
=E2=80=94 but before any <code>setTimeout</code> callbacks, ensuring predic=
table ordering. When building animation libraries or test utilities that as=
sert on DOM state after state updates, understanding the microtask/macrotas=
k boundary is essential for avoiding flaky assertions.</p>
