<p dir=3D"auto"><code>this</code> is a <strong>dynamic binding</strong> =E2=
=80=94 its value is determined at <strong>call time</strong>, not at defini=
tion time (unlike lexical scope). There are four binding rules, applied in =
order of precedence from highest to lowest:</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Priority</th>
<th>Rule</th>
<th>How triggered</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>1 (highest)</td>
<td><strong><code>new</code> binding</strong></td>
<td><code>new Foo()</code> =E2=80=94 <code>this</code> =3D the newly create=
d object</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>2</td>
<td><strong>Explicit binding</strong></td>
<td><code>.call(ctx)</code>, <code>.apply(ctx)</code>, <code>.bind(ctx)</co=
de> =E2=80=94 <code>this</code> =3D <code>ctx</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>3</td>
<td><strong>Implicit binding</strong></td>
<td><code>obj.method()</code> =E2=80=94 <code>this</code> =3D <code>obj</co=
de> (the object left of the dot)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>4 (lowest)</td>
<td><strong>Default binding</strong></td>
