<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>1. Native Objects</strong>:</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Are objects that are part of the JavaScript language define=
d by the ECMAScript specification. For example, <code>String</code>, <code>=
Math</code>, <code>RegExp</code>, <code>Object</code>, <code>Function</code=
> etc core objects defined in the ECMAScript spec.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>2. Host Objects</strong>:</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Are objects provided by the browser or runtime environment =
(Node). For example, <code>window</code>, <code>XmlHttpRequest</code>, <cod=
e>DOM nodes</code> etc considered as host objects.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>3. User Objects</strong>:</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Are objects defined in the javascript code. For example, Us=
er object created for profile information.</p>
