<p dir=3D"auto">In JavaScript, some built-in types (numbers, strings) are i=
mmutable, but custom objects are generally mutable. Some built-in immutable=
 JavaScript objects are <code>Math</code>, <code>Date</code>.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Here are a few ways to add/simulate immutability on plain J=
avaScript objects.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>1. Object Constant Properties:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">By combining <code>writable: false</code> and <code>configu=
rable: false</code>, you can essentially create a constant (cannot be chang=
