<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>1. Object:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">A data structure in which data is stored as key value pairs=
. In an object the key has to be a number, string, or symbol. The value can=
 be anything so also other objects, functions, etc. An object is a <strong>=
nonordered</strong> data structure, i.e. the sequence of insertion of key v=
alue pairs is not remembered.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Example:</strong></p>
