<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Key differences:</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>A <code>Map</code> is ordered and iterable, whereas a objects is not or=
dered and not iterable</li>
<li>We can put any type of data as a <code>Map</code> key, whereas objects =
can only have a number, string, or symbol as a key.</li>
<li>A <code>Map</code> inherits from <code>Map.prototype</code>. This offer=
s all sorts of utility functions and properties which makes working with <c=
ode>Map</code> objects a lot easier.</li>
</ul>
