<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Prototype pollution</strong> is a security vulnerab=
ility where an attacker is able to inject properties into a JavaScript obje=
ct's prototype (<code>Object.prototype</code>), causing those properties to=
 appear on <strong>every</strong> object in the application. This can lead =
to denial-of-service, property injection, or remote code execution.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>How it happens:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Many utility functions (deep merge, clone, set-by-path) use=
 bracket-notation assignment with user-controlled keys. If the key is <code=
>__proto__</code>, <code>constructor</code>, or <code>prototype</code>, the=
 attacker can modify <code>Object.prototype</code>.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Example:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative o=
verflow-auto" dir=3D"auto"><pre><span class=3D"pl-c">/**</span>
<span class=3D"pl-c"> * Vulnerable deep merge</span>
<span class=3D"pl-c"> */</span>

<span class=3D"pl-k">function</span> <span class=3D"pl-en">merge</span><spa=
n class=3D"pl-kos">(</span><span class=3D"pl-s1">target</span><span class=
=3D"pl-kos">,</span> <span class=3D"pl-s1">source</span><span class=3D"pl-k=
os">)</span> <span class=3D"pl-kos">{</span>
  <span class=3D"pl-k">for</span> <span class=3D"pl-kos">(</span><span clas=
s=3D"pl-k">const</span> <span class=3D"pl-s1">key</span> <span class=3D"pl-=
k">in</span> <span class=3D"pl-s1">source</span><span class=3D"pl-kos">)</s=
pan> <span class=3D"pl-kos">{</span>
    <span class=3D"pl-k">if</span> <span class=3D"pl-kos">(</span><span cla=
ss=3D"pl-k">typeof</span> <span class=3D"pl-s1">source</span><span class=3D=
"pl-kos">[</span><span class=3D"pl-s1">key</span><span class=3D"pl-kos">]</=
span> <span class=3D"pl-c1">=3D=3D=3D</span> <span class=3D"pl-s">'object'<=
