<p dir=3D"auto">The <code>Proxy</code> object allows to create an object th=
at can be used in place of the original object, but which may redefine fund=
amental <code>Object</code> operations like getting, setting, and defining =
properties via <strong>traps</strong> defined in a handler.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Proxy objects are commonly used to log property accesses, v=
alidate, format, or sanitize inputs, and so on.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Syntax:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative o=
verflow-auto" dir=3D"auto"><pre><span class=3D"pl-k">const</span> <span cla=
ss=3D"pl-s1">proxy</span> <span class=3D"pl-c1">=3D</span> <span class=3D"p=
