<p dir=3D"auto">An <strong>array</strong> is a specialised object for order=
ed, numerically-indexed data. An <strong>object</strong> is for named key-v=
alue pairs.</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th></th>
<th><code>[]</code> Array</th>
<th><code>{}</code> Object</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Keys</td>
<td>Numeric indices (0, 1, 2=E2=80=A6)</td>
<td>String / Symbol names</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Order</td>
<td>Guaranteed</td>
<td>Not guaranteed</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>.length</code></td>
<td>Yes</td>
<td>No</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Iteration</td>
<td><code>for...of</code>, <code>.forEach()</code></td>
<td><code>for...in</code>, <code>Object.keys()</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>typeof</code></td>
<td><code>"object"</code></td>
<td><code>"object"</code></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
