<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Real-World Use Case:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">RxJS operators are curried/partially applied functions =E2=
=80=94 <code>map(x =3D&gt; x * 2)</code> returns an operator function that,=
 when applied inside a <code>pipe()</code>, transforms an Observable. This =
design means operators are configuration-first, data-last =E2=80=94 identic=
al to curried functions. Ramda's entire library follows this convention: ev=
ery function is auto-curried and data is always the last argument, enabling=
 seamless point-free composition used in production at companies like Sound=
Cloud and Typeform.</p>
