<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Immutability</strong> means that once a data struct=
ure is created, it cannot be changed. Instead of mutating existing data, yo=
u produce new data with the desired changes. JavaScript does not enforce im=
mutability by default, but several mechanisms enforce it to varying degrees=
:</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Mechanism</th>
<th>Prevents new properties</th>
<th>Prevents property change</th>
<th>Prevents deletion</th>
<th>Deep?</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>const</code></td>
<td>(binding only)</td>
<td>No</td>
<td>No</td>
<td>No</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Object.freeze()</code></td>
<td>Yes</td>
<td>Yes</td>
<td>Yes</td>
<td>No (shallow)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Object.seal()</code></td>
<td>Yes</td>
<td>No</td>
<td>Yes</td>
<td>No</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Object.preventExtensions()</code></td>
<td>Yes</td>
<td>No</td>
<td>No</td>
<td>No</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Structural sharing (Immer/Immutable.js)</td>
<td>Yes (by convention/proxy)</td>
<td>Yes</td>
