<p dir=3D"auto">The Prototypal Inheritance is a feature in javascript used =
to add methods and properties in objects. It is a method by which an object=
 can inherit the properties and methods of another object.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">In order to get and set the [[Prototype]] of an object, we =
use <code>Object.getPrototypeOf()</code> and <code>Object.setPrototypeOf()<=
/code>. Nowadays, in modern language, it is being set using <code>__proto__=
</code>.</p>
