<p dir=3D"auto">Classes are a template for creating objects. They encapsula=
te data with code to work on that data. Classes in JS are built on prototyp=
es but also have some syntax and semantics that are not shared with ES5 cla=
ss-like semantics.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">ES6 Classes formalize the common JavaScript pattern of simu=
lating class-like inheritance hierarchies using functions and prototypes. T=
hey are effectively simple sugaring over prototype-based OO, offering a con=
venient declarative form for class patterns which encourage interoperabilit=
y.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">ES6 Class Properties</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Class keyword</li>
<li>getter/setter method</li>
<li>constructor function</li>
<li>extends keyword</li>
<li>super keyword</li>
<li>static keyword</li>
</ul>
