<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Prototype chaining</strong> is used to build new ty=
pes of objects based on existing ones. It is similar to inheritance in a cl=
ass based language. The prototype on object instance is available through <=
code>Object.getPrototypeOf(object)</code> or <code>__proto__</code> propert=
y whereas prototype on constructors function is available through <strong>O=
bject.prototype</strong>.</p>
