<p dir=3D"auto">ES6 <code>class</code> syntax is <strong>syntactic sugar</s=
trong> over JavaScript's existing prototype-based inheritance =E2=80=94 it =
does not introduce a new object model. Under the hood, a class declaration =
creates a constructor function and assigns methods to its <code>.prototype<=
/code>. Understanding this mapping is critical for debugging, performance p=
rofiling, and interoperating with pre-ES6 code.</p>
