<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Difference between Map and WeakMap:</strong></p>
<ol dir=3D"auto">
<li>A WeakMap accepts only <strong>objects</strong> as keys whereas a Map, =
in addition to <strong>objects</strong>, accepts primitive datatype such as=
 <strong>strings</strong>, <strong>numbers</strong> etc.</li>
<li>WeakMap objects doesn't avert garbage collection if there are no refere=
nces to the object which is acting like a key. Therefore there is no method=
 to retrieve keys in WeakMap, whereas in Map there are methods such as <cod=
e>Map.prototype.keys()</code> to get the keys.</li>
<li>There is no size property exists in WeakMap.</li>
</ol>
