<li>ParentNode.append() allows you to also append DOMString object, whereas=
 Node.appendChild() only accepts Node objects.</li>
<li>ParentNode.append() has no return value, whereas Node.appendChild() ret=
urns the appended Node object.</li>
<li>ParentNode.append() can append several nodes and strings, whereas Node.=
appendChild() can only append one node.</li>
</ul>
