<p dir=3D"auto">The <strong>Module pattern</strong> uses an IIFE (Immediate=
ly Invoked Function Expression) to create a private scope, exposing only a =
public API via the returned object. It predates ES6 and solves the problem =
of global namespace pollution in pre-module JavaScript environments.</p>
