<p dir=3D"auto">The <strong>singleton pattern</strong> is a type of creatio=
nal pattern that restricts the instantiation of a class to a <strong>single=
</strong> object. This allows the class to create an instance of the class =
the first time it is instantiated; however, on the next try, the existing i=
nstance of the class is returned. No new instance is created.</p>
<p align=3D"center" dir=3D"auto">
  <a target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" href=3D"https://github.c=
om/learning-zone/javascript-basics/blob/master/assets/singleton-pattern.png=
"><img src=3D"https://github.com/learning-zone/javascript-basics/raw/master=
/assets/singleton-pattern.png" alt=3D"Singleton Pattern" width=3D"400px" st=
yle=3D"max-width: 100%;"></a>
</p>
