<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>DRY vs. WET (Write Everything Twice):</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">DRY does not mean <em>never write similar-looking code</em>=
. Premature abstractions can introduce unnecessary coupling. A practical ru=
le: abstract duplication only when the same logic appears <strong>three or =
more times</strong> and the abstraction does not make the code harder to un=
derstand.</p>
