<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Component-based architecture</strong> is a design a=
pproach where the UI (and sometimes back-end logic) is broken into independ=
ent, reusable, self-contained <strong>components</strong>. Each component m=
anages its own structure (HTML), style (CSS), and behaviour (JavaScript).</=
p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Key characteristics:</strong></p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Principle</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Encapsulation</strong></td>
<td>A component owns its template, styles, and logic</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Reusability</strong></td>
<td>Components can be used in multiple places without modification</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Composability</strong></td>
<td>Complex UIs are built by composing simpler components</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Single responsibility</strong></td>
<td>Each component has one clear purpose</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Unidirectional data flow</strong></td>
<td>Data flows down via props; events bubble up</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
