<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF)</strong> is an at=
tack that forces an authenticated user to execute unwanted actions on a web=
 application where they are currently logged in. The attacker tricks the vi=
ctim's browser into making a malicious request to the target site, leveragi=
ng the session cookies automatically sent by the browser</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Attack flow:</strong></p>
<ol dir=3D"auto">
<li>Victim is logged into <code>bank.example.com</code> (session cookie set=
).</li>
<li>Victim visits <code>evil.com</code>, which contains <code>&lt;img src=
=3D"https://bank.example.com/transfer?to=3Dattacker&amp;amount=3D1000"&gt;<=
/code>.</li>
<li>Browser sends a GET request to <code>bank.example.com</code> with the v=
ictim's session cookie =E2=80=94 the bank processes the transfer.</li>
</ol>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Prevention strategies:</strong></p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Technique</th>
<th>How it works</th>
<th>Notes</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>CSRF Token</strong></td>
<td>Server issues a random per-session token; client includes it in every s=
tate-changing request; server validates</td>
<td>Classic; works for form-based apps</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>SameSite Cookie</strong></td>
<td><code>SameSite=3DStrict/Lax</code> =E2=80=94 browser does not send cook=
ie on cross-site requests</td>
<td>Best modern defence; <code>Lax</code> is now the default in Chrome</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Double Submit Cookie</strong></td>
<td>Token in cookie + request body/header; server checks they match</td>
<td>Stateless alternative to server-side token storage</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Custom Request Header</strong></td>
<td>API requires <code>X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest</code>; CORS blocks=
 cross-origin custom headers</td>
<td>Effective for AJAX APIs</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Origin / Referer validation</strong></td>
<td>Server checks <code>Origin</code> header matches its own domain</td>
<td>Defence-in-depth</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
