<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>XSS (Cross-Site Scripting):</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">XSS is an injection attack where an attacker injects malici=
ous scripts into content that is served to other users. The injected script=
 executes in the victim's browser with the same privileges as the trusted s=
ite.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Types of XSS:</strong></p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Type</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Stored XSS</td>
<td>Malicious script is persisted in the database and served to every user<=
/td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Reflected XSS</td>
<td>Script is included in the request and immediately reflected back in the=
 response</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>DOM-based XSS</td>
<td>Vulnerability exists entirely in the client-side code</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
