<p dir=3D"auto">The same-origin policy is a policy that prevents JavaScript=
 from making requests across domain boundaries. An origin is defined as a c=
ombination of URI scheme, hostname, and port number. If you enable this pol=
icy then it prevents a malicious script on one page from obtaining access t=
o sensitive data on another web page using Document Object Model(DOM).</p>
