<p dir=3D"auto">The <strong>browser rendering pipeline</strong> is the sequ=
ential process a browser engine follows to convert HTML, CSS, and JavaScrip=
t source code into actual pixels on a physical screen</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>The Rendering Pipeline Steps</strong></p>
<div class=3D"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overf=
low-auto"><pre class=3D"notranslate"><code>HTML parsing =E2=86=92 DOM Tree
CSS parsing  =E2=86=92 CSSOM Tree
               =E2=86=93
           Render Tree (DOM + CSSOM =E2=80=94 only visible nodes)
               =E2=86=93
           Layout (Reflow) =E2=80=94 computes geometry: position, size, box=
 model
               =E2=86=93
           Paint =E2=80=94 rasterises each layer to pixel bitmaps
               =E2=86=93
           Compositing =E2=80=94 GPU assembles layers in correct order
